// =============================================================================
// equilibrium.mx3.in -- equilibrium-state template. Placeholders are filled in by
// mumax3_script.render_equilibrium_script; rendered and executed once per parameter
// set: process working directory = equilibrium/, rendered script fixed name
// equilibrium.mx3; MuMax3 default native output directory equilibrium.out/
// (contract-required: equilibrium.ovf); run.log is written by the pipeline at the
// equilibrium/ root. Produces the equilibrium.ovf shared by all pulses.
// Command syntax follows the MuMax3 3.12 official API documentation; the execution
// chain has been minimally validated by a short test-only pilot (8x4x1, 1 pulse,
// 3 samples). The numerical protocol (EdgeSmooth/solver/MaxErr/MaxDt/GammaLL/
// RelaxTorqueThreshold) is explicitly injected from the YAML numerics block;
// diagnostics (geom.ovf snapshot and DIAGNOSTIC stdout lines) go to the native
// output directory and run.log; convergence/QC validation remains to be done, and
// until then this must not be used for formal research data.
// Physical assumptions are in README.md at the repository root: 0 K, single uniform
// material, flat-ellipsoid thin nano-magnet, demag enabled, open boundaries without
// PBC, no DMI, no STT, no static bias field.
// =============================================================================

// 1. Shared model section: numerical protocol (EdgeSmooth/SetSolver/MaxErr/MaxDt/
//    GammaLL) plus the single rendering of grid/ellipsoid geometry/Msat/Aex/Ku1/
//    easy axis/demag/open boundaries (_render_model_setup), byte-identical to the
//    shared section of simulation.mx3.in; cell_size is derived from size_m/cells and
//    filled in; alpha and RelaxTorqueThreshold are not part of the shared section.
{{MODEL_SETUP}}

// 2. Uniform initial state: fixed initial direction (the initial state is not
//    changed afterwards)
m = uniform({{INIT_M}})

// 3. Diagnostic snapshot: geometry voxelization (SetGeom already done in the shared
//    section) -> equilibrium.out/geom.ovf
SaveAs(geom, "geom")

// 4. Zero-field equilibration (once only; no static bias field, B_ext is identically
//    0). RelaxTorqueThreshold is rendered from the YAML numerics block in T; -1 keeps
//    the official default (stop once the average torque plateaus/increases). Relax
//    may temporarily switch the solver internally and restores the user SetSolver
//    configuration afterwards.
B_ext = vector(0, 0, 0)
RelaxTorqueThreshold = {{RELAX_TORQUE_THRESHOLD_T}}
relax_converged := Relax()
// Diagnostics go to run.log via stdout (DIAGNOSTIC prefix for easy lookup);
// MaxTorque is in T, E_total in J, step/NEval are integer counts.
print("DIAGNOSTIC relax_converged=", relax_converged, " MaxTorque_T=", MaxTorque, " E_total_J=", E_total, " step=", step, " NEval=", NEval)

// 5. Save the shared equilibrium state: written to the default native output
//    directory, i.e. equilibrium.out/equilibrium.ovf
SaveAs(m, "equilibrium")
